WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.629
Pharmacare.

00:00:01.579 --> 00:00:07.704
Canada is the only country with universal healthcare that does not include universal prescription drug coverage.

00:00:07.704 --> 00:00:12.863
The Hoskins Advisory Council recommended national pharmacare in 2019.

00:00:12.863 --> 00:00:19.954
Bill C-64 received Royal Assent in October 2024 for diabetes and contraception coverage only.

00:00:19.954 --> 00:00:22.943
Full implementation remains years away.

00:00:22.943 --> 00:00:27.977
Meanwhile, one in five Canadians report not filling prescriptions due to cost.

00:00:27.977 --> 00:00:29.295
The gap.

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:34.056
Every other country with universal healthcare includes prescription drug coverage.

00:00:34.056 --> 00:00:35.852
Canada does not.

00:00:35.852 --> 00:00:42.556
Coverage depends on employer insurance, provincial programs with varying eligibility, or ability to pay out-of-pocket.

00:00:42.556 --> 00:00:47.681
The result: one in five Canadians report not filling prescriptions due to cost.

00:00:47.681 --> 00:00:53.181
The Hoskins Advisory Council recommended full universal pharmacare in 2019.

00:00:53.181 --> 00:00:59.454
Seven years later, only diabetes medications and contraception are covered under the new federal program.

00:00:59.454 --> 00:01:01.795
The implementation pattern.

00:01:01.795 --> 00:01:04.443
Promise a transformational program.

00:01:04.443 --> 00:01:07.795
Commission a report recommending full implementation.

00:01:07.795 --> 00:01:09.647
Accept the report.

00:01:09.647 --> 00:01:11.295
Wait years.

00:01:11.295 --> 00:01:15.340
Pass limited legislation covering a fraction of the original vision.

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:18.306
Announce the fraction as a historic achievement.

00:01:18.306 --> 00:01:21.306
Defer full implementation indefinitely.

00:01:21.306 --> 00:01:29.874
This is the same pattern as the Canada Disability Benefit: announced as transformational, implemented at two hundred dollars per month below the poverty line.
